      ],
      "explanation": "To find a minimum, rewrite the expression as a square plus a constant. Since\n\\[\n(2x-3)^2=4x^2-12x+9,\n\\]\nwe have\n\\[\n4x^2-12x-1=(2x-3)^2-10.\n\\]\nFor every real \\(x\\), the square is nonnegative, so the function is at least \\(-10\\). This value is attained when \\(2x-3=0\\), or \\(x=\\tfrac32\\). Hence its minimum value is \\(\\boxed{-10}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
      "id": "complete-the-square",
